    "text": "By Kalyn ,\n15 hours ago Richardson, Texas — a city where the sun bounces off mid-century brick and glass, where the scent of cumin and lime drifts through neighborhoods stitched together by families from every corner of the globe. Here, the DART trains hum past taquerias and tech campuses alike, and the air is alive with the laughter of students, the quiet pride of shopkeepers, the sizzle of something delicious on the grill. Richardson is a crossroads — of cultures, of cuisines, of stories told over plates passed hand to hand. Read full article\n1",
